# Kit's UI, described in Kit's own notation — the other half of kit.beh.
#
# kit:project kit
#   kit#237: Kit is one project. This file is its browser UI; Kit shows the three files
#   as ONE page whose features are its pages and areas, never the files (kit#246),
#   while check and report still read each file on its own.
#
# kit:self-authored
#   Read by saturation.js, which excludes this corpus from the binding-saturation
#   study. None of its other three axes is true here: this describes a UI, for
#   software that exists, and no other corpus in that study describes this app.
#   The disqualifying property is different — the app, this corpus and its
#   bindings share ONE author, written in one sitting with the bindings already
#   in mind. The measurement caught it before the argument did: every other
#   corpus scores 59–76% against the shuffled null and this one scored 10%, the
#   only one that looks like it saturates faster than chance. That is the author,
#   not the app. The study's claim is an independence claim, so this corpus
#   cannot be evidence for it — which says nothing about the corpus itself.
#
# ── Why this is a SECOND corpus and not more of kit.beh ──────────────────────
# `kit.beh` declares `# kit:no-ui` and its 0% is not a gap, it is EVIDENCE: Kit
# the command-line tool needs `runs`, `exits`, `reports`, `raises`, and the
# generator's whole vocabulary is browser verbs. Adding browser behaviours to
# that file would dilute the one measurement that makes the point.
#
# So Kit is two apps in its own registry, and only one of them has a UI.
#
# ── What this file is FOR ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# kit.beh's header states a falsifiable claim: *"this file is not a corpus that
# is waiting for bindings… the missing piece is not notation, it is a UI. That
# is the same UI James asked for in the first half of #89."*
#
# That UI now exists (kit#16 → #24 → #26 → #27 → #28). This corpus is the test
# of the claim: if it was right, a browser corpus of Kit's own surface should
# derive real Playwright, and Kit stops being a special case in its own
# registry. If it was wrong, this file says so at the same cost.
#
# ⚠️ **THE CONFOUND, STATED FIRST.** I built this UI, so a corpus I write about
# it measures recall as much as description — the same objection that made
# kit#23 use two isolated agents. It does NOT undermine the question being asked
# here, which is whether the GENERATOR can emit a runnable test for a browser
# surface, not whether two authors would pick the same nouns. That second
# question is kit#23's and is still open. Read the derived count as evidence
# about the generator, never about the notation's learnability.
#
# ── Nouns are prefixed `Kit*`, and they no longer need to be ─────────────────
# THE REASON IS GONE AS OF claude-code-bot#66 (2026-09-25). The old bindings file
# warned that THE NOUN NAMESPACE IS GLOBAL ACROSS APPS: an unprefixed `page:Home`
# here would silently reuse snip-it's binding and emit `page.goto('./')` — a test
# that RUNS, against the wrong app, with no unbound-noun warning. James ended
# that; a corpus now binds its own nouns in `kit-ui.bindings.json` beside this
# file, so the collision cannot occur.
#
# The prefixes are therefore harmless history rather than a rule, and they stay:
# renaming a noun is a change to the CORPUS and his to make (claude-code-bot#58),
# not a tidy-up. Do NOT tell the next corpus to copy the habit.
#
# Every accessible name below was READ OFF THE RUNNING APP, not invented — the
# same rule every bindings file holds itself to.
#
# ⚠️ Ids here are NOT `BEH-UI-*`, deliberately. `kit.beh` already uses that
# prefix for four behaviours of the ui.js SERVER — the loopback bind, the
# traversal refusal, the method-not-allowed handler. Same spelling, different
# subject, and one file away from each other. Ids are corpus-scoped so nothing
# would have broken; a reader would simply have been wrong.

# ═══ Features: the pages, and the parts on more than one (kit#237) ═══════════
# Each page is a feature, and a part shown on several pages is a feature in each of
# them: the notes panel sits on the project page and the behaviour page, and the
# schedule on the project page and the board. A tag says where a behaviour is
# SHOWN; it is not a dependency (that is `serves`).

feature FEAT-NAV "Navbar"
  stage development
feature FEAT-PROJECTS "Project list"
  stage ui
feature FEAT-PROJECT "Project page"
  stage development
feature FEAT-BEHAVIOUR "Behaviour page"
  stage ui
feature FEAT-BOARD "Board"
  stage development
feature FEAT-FEATURE "Feature page"
  stage ui

feature FEAT-NOTES "Notes"
  stage development
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  in FEAT-BEHAVIOUR

feature FEAT-SCHEDULE "Schedule"
  stage ui
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  in FEAT-BOARD

behaviour BEH-LIST-1 "Every corpus Kit can read is listed as a project"
  in FEAT-PROJECTS
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProjects
  then sees heading:KitProjectsTitle
  then sees region:KitMain
  contract a corpus that will not parse is listed AS an error, not as zero behaviours

# ═══ Scheduled vs backlog (kit#118) ══════════════════════════════════════════
# "maybe there is a point where things are scheduled vs backlogged and the
# schedule is ordered … and the backlog is just an idea to happen at some point
# but not a candidate for execution for now." A `pending` behaviour is already
# an unbuilt one; this splits the pending set in two. Backlog is the default, so
# no existing corpus changes meaning. Estimated delivery is his "later" — not here.
# Built 2026-10-14 in the shape kit#231 proposed (his default lapsed unreshaped).

behaviour BEH-SCHED-1 "A project lists its scheduled behaviours in order, apart from its backlog"
  in FEAT-SCHEDULE
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  then sees region:KitSchedule
  then sees region:KitBacklog
  contract the schedule is an ordered list of pending behaviour ids in <app>.schedule beside the corpus
  contract a pending behaviour not on the schedule is backlog; nothing in the .beh says which
  contract a built behaviour is never listed in either, and an id on the schedule that is no longer pending is shown as done, not dropped silently

behaviour BEH-SCHED-2 "A backlog behaviour can be scheduled, and the schedule reordered"
  in FEAT-SCHEDULE
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  when activates button:KitScheduleBehaviour
  then sees region:KitSchedule
  contract scheduling appends to the end of the schedule; moving up or down swaps neighbours
  contract unscheduling returns it to the backlog; no behaviour is deleted by either
  contract each change is committed and pushed like any other edit, and the write result says so

behaviour BEH-SCHED-3 "The next behaviour to build is the top of the schedule"
  in FEAT-SCHEDULE
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  then sees region:KitSchedule
  contract the first still-pending id on the schedule is marked next — the one an agent picks up
  contract with nothing scheduled the region says so, and does not fall back to the backlog

behaviour BEH-SHEET-1 "A project shows the question sheet Kit built for it"
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  actor engineer
  provides page:KitProject.app = james-habits-app
  when opens page:KitProject
  when activates tab:KitProjectQuestionsTab
  then sees heading:KitQuestionSheet
  then sees heading:KitNeverAdjudicated
  then sees button:KitAskForBehaviour

behaviour BEH-SHEET-2 "The Questions tab leads with what Kit is asking him, and calls the rest problems"
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  layer ux
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-22-2248
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  when activates tab:KitProjectQuestionsTab
  then sees heading:KitAsking
  then sees heading:KitQuestionSheet
  contract "The questions tab doesn't really show questions at the moment it kind of just shows probelms" (kit.notes.md, 2026-10-22 22:46Z)
  contract "I think kit it is important that kit starts to raise the questions which helps guide the user in the right direction. Right now I'm not sure what ux ui or logic to define to unblock kit"
  contract first on the tab, under "Kit is asking you": every needs-context line on a card still to build and not paused (BEH-BOARD-17), and every review request whose note is a question (BEH-BOARD-11); the question is in bold, with the card it is about beneath it as a link
  contract the old Question sheet heading reads "Problems in the spec": conflicts and never-adjudicated inferences are problems Kit found, not questions
  contract the tab's count includes the questions, so a project with only questions still shows a count
  contract each needs-context line is one answerable question that ends with what the agent does if he never answers, so silence is a decision rather than a block (the agent's practice since kit#413)
  contract he answers under the question itself (BEH-SHEET-3), or on the card as for any review

behaviour BEH-SHEET-3 "He can answer what Kit is asking, under the question"
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  layer ux
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-22-2347
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  when activates tab:KitProjectQuestionsTab
  when fills field:KitReply with "invite-only to start"
  when activates button:KitReply
  then sees heading:KitAsking
  contract "Kit is asking you needs a way to reply" (kit.notes.md, 2026-10-22 23:47Z)
  contract every question under "Kit is asking you" has an answer box and a Reply button; nothing is sent while the box is blank
  contract an answer is a plain note on the card the question is about, in the notes the page shows, so the agent reads and folds it like any other note
  contract until it is folded, his answer shows under the question, marked as waiting for Kit, and the box becomes "Add to your answer"
  contract my assumption: the question stays on the tab until the agent acts on his answer and edits or removes the card's needs-context line, so an answer is never lost between his reply and the agent's next wake

behaviour BEH-PAIR-1 "A behaviour and the test Kit generates from it are on one screen"
  in FEAT-BEHAVIOUR
  actor engineer
  provides page:KitBehaviour.app = james-habits-app
  provides page:KitBehaviour.id = BEH-SEED-1
  when opens page:KitBehaviour
  then sees heading:KitBehaviourSteps
  then sees heading:KitGeneratedTest
  contract the two are side by side, not on separate screens — the output must be in view
  contract the test is regenerated on every read, never cached

behaviour BEH-ADJ-1 "An inference can be adjudicated from the browser"
  in FEAT-BEHAVIOUR
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBehaviour
  then sees heading:KitAdjudication
  then sees button:KitApprove
  when activates button:KitApprove
  contract the corpus file on disk gains `review approved` for this behaviour
  contract the existing `review unreviewed` line is REPLACED, not joined by a second
  contract nothing is committed to git

behaviour BEH-ADJ-2 "Denying an inference asks for the correction it must carry"
  in FEAT-BEHAVIOUR
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBehaviour
  then sees button:KitDeny
  when fills field:KitCorrection with "the starter set is re-seeded whenever the list is empty"
  when activates button:KitDeny
  contract Deny is disabled while the correction is empty
  contract a denial with no correction is refused by the parser, and its sentence reaches the screen

behaviour BEH-STEP-1 "A step can be added while the generated test is in view"
  in FEAT-BEHAVIOUR
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBehaviour
  then sees heading:KitAddAStep
  then sees button:KitAddStep
  contract the page re-reads after the write, so the REGENERATED test is what is on screen

# ═══ Free-text notes (kit#118) ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
# "a less structured input in the ui where you can just comment on something
# rather than defining a behaviour and this follows the workflow to get folded
# into the spec and code" — and, 2026-10-10: "I want to be using kit but it just
# isn't quite natural yet". A note is NOT a behaviour: nothing parses it, and
# nothing generates from it. It is an inbox the engineer empties into the spec.
# Built in the same stack as this spec; the shape is his to change (kit#118, default 10-11).

behaviour BEH-GATE-H2 "Every box that writes a note says it will be public, before it is sent"
  in FEAT-NOTES
  source inferred claude-code-bot#35
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  then sees region:KitOpenNotes
  contract reads are served to anyone by decision (BEH-GATE-H1), and a note is committed to a public repository, so the lock does not make a note private
  contract one line under the note box, the ask-for-behaviour box on the project page, and the board's box; replies are not covered yet
  contract my assumption: worded "Public: this is saved to Kit's GitHub repository, which anyone can read." He can deny the line or change the wording

behaviour BEH-NOTE-1 "A note can be left on a project without writing a behaviour"
  in FEAT-NOTES
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  when fills field:KitNote with "the habit list should remember the order I dragged it into"
  when activates button:KitLeaveNote
  then sees region:KitOpenNotes
  contract the note is appended to <app>.notes.md beside the corpus, never into the .beh
  contract it is committed and pushed like any other edit, and the write result says so
  contract Leave note is disabled while the box is empty

behaviour BEH-NOTE-2 "A note left on a behaviour names that behaviour"
  in FEAT-NOTES
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBehaviour
  when fills field:KitNote with "this should also cover the empty list"
  when activates button:KitLeaveNote
  contract the note carries the behaviour's id, so it is listed under the project too
  contract the note survives the behaviour being renamed or removed — it is text, not a link

behaviour BEH-NOTE-3 "A note is removed in the change that folds it into the spec"
  in FEAT-NOTES
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  then sees region:KitOpenNotes
  contract <app>.notes.md holds only notes nobody has folded yet; a folded note is deleted,
  contract not ticked, in the same pull request that adds the behaviour or code it became
  contract with no open notes the region says so, rather than vanishing

# ═══ Free text in place of forms (kit#118, 2026-10-12) ═══════════════════════
# "the way that you define behaviours is quite a chore at the moment I really like
# the note style input … I am thinking more free form text inputs. In place of the
# behaviour input for example." And: "some ui to show rejected free form text if
# the ai can't decode the intention, maybe with some directed questions … or
# dismiss", and "Question where need a resolution input. This could be free form
# text as well". So every input that asked for structure asks for prose instead,
# and the structure is written by whoever folds the note. Who folds it — the agent
# on its next wake, or a model call inside Kit — is open (kit#118); these screens
# are the same either way. `pending` until built; the shape is his to change.

behaviour BEH-NOTE-4 "A new behaviour is asked for in free text, not a form"
  in FEAT-NOTES
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  when fills field:KitDescribeBehaviour with "dragging a habit reorders the list and it stays that way"
  when activates button:KitAskForBehaviour
  then sees region:KitOpenNotes
  contract it is saved as a request note in <app>.notes.md; the corpus is not touched until it is folded
  contract no id, title or actor is asked for — whoever folds it writes those, and the steps
  contract Ask for behaviour is disabled while the box is empty

behaviour BEH-NOTE-5 "A note that could not be turned into spec comes back with questions"
  in FEAT-NOTES
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  then sees region:KitNeedsAnswer
  contract whoever folds a note it cannot decode leaves it open and writes numbered questions under it
  contract the questions are in a form a note's own text cannot forge, so prose never reads as a question
  contract notes with questions are listed above every other open note, newest question first
  contract with none waiting there is no region at all — an empty one on every project page is the scrolling he asked to lose
  contract a note waiting on an answer is listed only there, never again among the open notes

behaviour BEH-NOTE-6 "A note's questions are answered in free text"
  in FEAT-NOTES
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  when fills field:KitReply with "only on the today view, the history keeps date order"
  when activates button:KitReply
  then sees region:KitOpenNotes
  contract the reply is appended under the note and its questions; the note stays open for the next fold
  contract it is committed and pushed like any other edit, and the write result says so

behaviour BEH-NOTE-7 "A note can be dismissed"
  in FEAT-NOTES
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  when activates button:KitDismiss
  then sees region:KitOpenNotes
  contract the note leaves <app>.notes.md in a commit of its own; git history keeps it, so dismissing is recoverable
  contract it asks nothing further — dismiss is the cancel, and a second prompt would make it a chore again
  contract dismissing a note that someone else already removed says so, rather than failing silently

behaviour BEH-NOTE-8 "A decision on the question sheet is resolved in free text"
  in FEAT-NOTES
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  when fills field:KitResolution with "BEH-CUT-2 wins; a cut is always downloadable"
  when activates button:KitResolve
  then sees region:KitOpenNotes
  contract it leaves a note tagged with the decision's key; the conflict stays on the sheet until the note is folded
  contract no corpus keyword is invented to record it — the fold is what edits the behaviours

behaviour BEH-TITLE-1 "A behaviour is shown by its title, its id kept small"
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  in FEAT-BEHAVIOUR
  in FEAT-BOARD
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  contract every card leads with the title; the id follows in muted type, still there to search and link by
  contract an id is never removed from a URL or a commit — it is quieter, not gone

# ═══ Navigation and the board (kit#237) ═══════════════════════════════════════
# "What I am seeing is more like an agile tool … a navbar with two views for now:
# board view and project view." The project view is the existing pages until the
# feature model is decided (kit#237). The board's columns map onto what the corpus
# already says: proposed = an inference nobody has adjudicated, backlog = pending,
# done = built. Scheduled and in progress are not in the .beh: they read each
# file's schedule (BEH-SCHED, BEH-BOARD-3). Nor is when a behaviour was done:
# BEH-BOARD-4 reads that from git, through GET /api/projects/<app>/history.

behaviour BEH-NAV-1 "Every page carries a navbar with the board and the projects"
  in FEAT-NAV
  source defined kit#237
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProjects
  then sees region:KitNav
  when activates link:KitNavBoard
  then sees heading:KitBoardTitle
  contract the navbar marks the view you are on; the projects link is the existing project list

behaviour BEH-BOARD-1 "The board shows every behaviour in a column for where it stands"
  in FEAT-BOARD
  source defined kit#237
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  then sees region:KitBoardProposed
  then sees region:KitBoardBacklog
  then sees region:KitBoardDone
  contract proposed is source inferred and review unreviewed; pending is Backlog, Queue, Blocked or In progress (BEH-BOARD-18); done is everything else
  contract a denied inference is on no column — it is not work, it is a correction waiting to be written
  contract each card is the behaviour's id and title, links to its behaviour page, and names its project
  contract a corpus that will not parse is named on the board as an error, never silently left out

behaviour BEH-BOARD-2 "Cards are coloured by project, and the board can be filtered to projects"
  in FEAT-BOARD
  source defined kit#237
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  when activates button:KitBoardShowTrials
  then sees region:KitBoardBacklog
  contract a project keeps the same colour on every visit; the filter lives in the url so it can be shared
  contract trial corpora (not-a-real-app, duplicate-corpus) are hidden until asked for

behaviour BEH-BOARD-3 "An in-progress column sits before done"
  in FEAT-BOARD
  in FEAT-SCHEDULE
  source defined kit#237
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  then sees region:KitBoardInProgress
  contract in progress is the top of the project's schedule, the one marked next (BEH-SCHED-3)
  contract it waits on BEH-SCHED; until it is built it is not drawn, rather than drawn empty
  contract the Scheduled column this once named went with BEH-BOARD-18 (his 2026-10-22 22:37Z note: "Lets ditch scheduled"); the rest of a schedule waits in the Queue

behaviour BEH-BOARD-4 "Done is ordered most recently completed first"
  in FEAT-BOARD
  source defined kit#237
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  then sees region:KitBoardDone
  contract completed is when the behaviour last stopped being pending, read from git history, not stored in the .beh
  contract a behaviour with no history (never pending) is completed when it was added

behaviour BEH-BOARD-5 "Proposed and backlog put the top priority at the top"
  in FEAT-BOARD
  source defined kit#284
  priority 2
  review approved
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  then sees region:KitBoardProposed
  then sees region:KitBoardBacklog
  contract a `priority` line ranks a card 1 (first) to 5, across projects; a card with none comes after every ranked one
  contract the score is shown on the card, so the order can be read without opening anything
  contract it is how the agent's suggestions reach the top: an unreviewed inference with `priority 1` leads Proposed

behaviour BEH-BOARD-6 "Review requested comes first: built work the agent wants looked at, top priority at the top"
  in FEAT-BOARD
  source defined kit#284
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  then sees region:KitBoardReview
  contract a `review requested <what to look at>` line puts a behaviour here whatever else is true of it, and the card says what
  contract approving it moves it on (built is Done); denying it needs the correction, like any denial, and takes it off the board
  contract it is how built-and-merged work asks for his eyes without blocking on them

behaviour BEH-IDEA-1 "App ideas have their own page in the navbar, and are never on the board"
  in FEAT-NAV
  in FEAT-BOARD
  source defined kit#284
  priority 2
  review approved
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  then sees link:KitNavIdeas
  contract the Ideas page is the `ideas` project: one `# kit:idea` file whose features are the ideas
  contract a ramble is a note on it, and the agent folds rambles into that idea's behaviours
  contract it is off the board and the project list even with trials shown: an idea is not work until it graduates to its own <app>.beh

behaviour BEH-PRIN-1 "Principles have their own page in the navbar: global ones first, then each project's own"
  in FEAT-NAV
  source defined kit#284
  priority 2
  review approved
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  then sees link:KitNavPrinciples
  contract a principle lives in the corpus it governs, as a `# kit:principle [global] <Name>: <what it means>` line; `global` means it holds for every project
  contract the project page shows its own principles; the Principles page gathers every project's, global first, and names the line each lives on
  contract a note on the project is how he changes one; the agent edits the line
  contract the Ideas file is never read for principles: an idea is not a project

behaviour BEH-BOARD-7 "A long column shows its top ten, and more on request"
  in FEAT-BOARD
  source defined kit#284
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  then sees region:KitBoardBacklog
  contract capped after sorting, so what is hidden is always the bottom of the column's order
  contract the header still counts every card, and the button says how many it will show and how many are hidden

# ═══ The projects view: features, and parents as tags (kit#237) ═══════════════
# "Features can parent other features, they can also parent spec … consider the
# parent relationships as tags … a feature can be a sub feature of multiple
# features." Decided on kit#237 (2026-10-11); the language is in
# docs/design/features.md. `feature FEAT-X "title"` declares a feature, and an
# `in FEAT-X` line on a feature or a behaviour tags it under a parent — repeat
# the line for several parents. Nothing has to be tagged: a corpus with no
# features is shown exactly as it was, as a flat list.

behaviour BEH-FEAT-1 "A project shows its top-level features, then its untagged behaviours"
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  source defined kit#237
  actor engineer
  provides page:KitProject.app = kit-ui
  when opens page:KitProject
  then sees region:KitProjectFeatures
  contract top level is every feature and every behaviour with no `in` line
  contract a feature card names its title and how many behaviours sit anywhere beneath it, each counted once
  contract a project with no features shows its behaviours as it always has

behaviour BEH-FEAT-2 "A feature shows its child features, its behaviours, and every parent as a tag"
  in FEAT-FEATURE
  source defined kit#237
  actor engineer
  provides page:KitFeature.app = kit-ui
  provides page:KitFeature.id = FEAT-NOTES
  when opens page:KitFeature
  then sees region:KitFeatureChildren
  then sees region:KitFeatureParents
  contract a child is anything with an `in` line naming this feature; one thing tagged into two features is listed under both
  contract each parent links to its own feature page; none of them is the owner

behaviour BEH-FEAT-3 "The breadcrumb is the path you came by"
  in FEAT-FEATURE
  source defined kit#237
  actor engineer
  provides page:KitFeature.app = kit-ui
  provides page:KitFeature.id = FEAT-NOTES
  when opens page:KitFeature
  then sees region:KitBreadcrumb
  contract with several parents there is no single path, so the path is carried in the url and a shared link shows the same crumbs
  contract with no path in the url the crumbs are the project and the feature, never a parent picked for you

behaviour BEH-FEAT-4 "Files naming the same project are one card, with one link"
  in FEAT-PROJECTS
  source defined kit#246
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProjects
  then sees region:KitProjectList
  contract `# kit:project <name>` groups files on the project list and the board; the card links to the project's one page and lists no file
  contract a file without the directive is its own project, as today; check and report still read one file at a time

behaviour BEH-FEAT-5 "A project of several files is one page, its features drawn from every file"
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  source defined kit#246
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  then sees region:KitProjectFeatures
  contract top level is every file's top-level features and untagged behaviours together, under no heading that names a file
  contract each feature and behaviour links into the file it lives in; the counts are the sum over the files

# His Kit note, 2026-10-12 20:49Z, left on page:KitProject: "Maybe features and
# questions should be under a tab view, default to features".
behaviour BEH-FEAT-6 "A project's features and questions are two tabs, features first"
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  source defined kit#118
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  then sees tab:KitProjectFeaturesTab
  then sees tab:KitProjectQuestionsTab
  contract features is the selected tab unless the url says ?tab=questions, so a link can open on the questions
  contract the questions tab carries the count of conflicts and questions waiting, so nothing waits unseen behind it
  contract the ask box sits above the tabs; the notes are a tab of their own (BEH-FEAT-7)

# ═══ His Kit notes, 2026-10-16 07:13–07:30Z ════════════════════════════════════
# "Let's leverage the tab view more", "Are ui/ux/logic implementation even treated
# as tags right now … Let's get that implemented", "Notes should be ordered most
# recently written at the top", "Boards could probably have a free form text input",
# "Could we move towards a shadcn style ui?", and "these notes are being wrapped into
# kit spec right?". Each behaviour below names the note it folds in its source line,
# which is what BEH-NOTE-10 reads. Where I had to choose a shape, the build marks it
# `review requested` so he can say no in Kit.

behaviour BEH-FEAT-7 "The describe box sits above the tabs, and notes are a tab of their own"
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  in FEAT-NOTES
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-16-0713
  priority 1
  review approved
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitProject
  then sees tab:KitProjectNotesTab
  contract above the tabs is only the title, its badges and the describe box, so asking never needs a tab
  contract the Notes tab holds the notes needing an answer, the open notes and the edits waiting to land; its label counts the open notes
  contract the schedule is a tab, and so are principles when the project has any
  contract asking for a behaviour opens the Notes tab, so the note just left is in view

behaviour BEH-NOTE-9 "Notes are listed newest first, ten at a time"
