  priority 2
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitBoard
  then sees region:KitNav
  contract the shadcn look: neutral greys, thin borders, a small radius, even whitespace, and colour kept for meaning
  contract the look, not the library: Kit draws on the design-system package, and swapping that is a platform choice that stays his
  contract every gap between blocks comes from one spacing scale, so a page has no one-off margins
  contract my assumption: the page sets the gap, not the block; each block in a page sits one step below the last, a section heading opens a wider gap, and what follows a title sits closer (index.css, `.app main > * + *`)
  contract my assumption: a utility action (Edit, Cancel, Keep it, Show more, Ring the bell) is an outlined ghost button, so the only filled buttons on a page are its main action and a danger; teal stays only where it means selected (the board's filter chips)
  contract built in kit#376, kit#377 and kit#379; a test now holds the spacing scale, so it leaves the Backlog (kit#388)

behaviour BEH-LOOK-2 "Kit wears the design system's professional theme, and a title that links reads as a title"
