# ═══ Feature stages (kit.notes.md 2026-10-19 08:23Z) ═════════════════════════
# "a board view which enforces the feature creation pipeline. Let's make this
# separate from the existing board for now and we can unify them later if it
# makes sense before public release". Ids are STAGE, not PIPELINE: snip-it.beh
# already has a FEAT-PIPELINE for its video board, and one word meaning two
# boards a corpus apart is the trap the BEH-UI note above describes.
#
# A feature's stage lives in the corpus as `stage <problem|ux|logic|development|ui>`
# under its `feature` line: a corpus LANGUAGE change (claude-code-bot#58), which he
# approved on BEH-STAGE-1 at 2026-10-19 13:39Z. Built: BEH-STAGE-1, -2, -3 and -8
# (-2 on 2026-10-21: every feature in the real corpora got a stage line; split into
# FEAT-STAGE-READING on 2026-10-22). The agent's other halves (-5, -6) were closed
# on 2026-10-22 (kit#401) with the evidence written on each.

feature FEAT-STAGES "Feature stages"
  stage development

behaviour BEH-STAGE-1 "A separate board takes every feature through five stages: problem, UX, logic, development, UI"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  priority 2
  review approved
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract the stages, in order: problem statement, UX requirements, business logic, development, UI requirements
  contract separate from the behaviour board (FEAT-BOARD) for now; unifying the two is a later call, before a public release
  contract a column per stage, a card per feature, coloured by project as the behaviour board's are

# Was BEH-STAGE-2, "The agent puts each feature at a rough stage, read from how much
# of its spec is written and how much is built". Rewritten from his 16:16Z note (the
# stage is the agent's rough reading of the spec and the code, not a gate he fills),
# then split into this feature when he approved the split on 2026-10-22 11:20Z
# (BEH-EPIC-9). Its contracts moved into the three children below, unchanged.
feature FEAT-STAGE-READING "The agent reads each feature's stage"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  stage ui

behaviour BEH-STAGE-9 "The stage board is for reading: the agent writes every stage line, and he never moves a card"
  in FEAT-STAGE-READING
  source inferred kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  source inferred kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-1616
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract "used by the bot to group features into a rough completion stage based off the provided spec that the dev has filled in and implementation state"
  contract "the human can use it to quickly identify what work is left to be done": the board is for reading, and he never has to move a card
  contract every feature goes through the stages; a simple one just needs less written at each, and a one-line answer is enough
  contract the agent writes the stage line and moves it on when it rereads the feature; "rough" means a stage can lag the spec by a wake

behaviour BEH-STAGE-10 "A feature with anything built sits at development, or at ui once all of it is built"
  in FEAT-STAGE-READING
  source inferred kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-1616
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract my assumption: a feature with every behaviour built is at ui, since UI is the stage that stays open after development (BEH-STAGE-4); one with some built is at development
  contract my assumption: engine features with no screen (kit.beh's parser, writer, server) still go to ui when built, so the board reads "nothing left but polish"
  contract a build is never "rough": a feature with a built behaviour still at problem, ux or logic turns the suite red. On 2026-10-22 that caught FEAT-COMMENTS, built the day before and left at problem

behaviour BEH-STAGE-11 "A feature with nothing built is placed by reading it"
  in FEAT-STAGE-READING
  source inferred kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-1616
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract my assumption: problem for one-line ideas, ux for who-does-what steps, logic once its rules are written
  contract built by the agent's reading, so no test can say a placement is right; BEH-STAGE-9's test holds only that one is written

behaviour BEH-STAGE-3 "Development is iterative and runs through the spec: behaviours are added and refined until they are built"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  priority 3
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract a feature in development shows its behaviours' progress, built out of total, from the same counts the project page uses

behaviour BEH-STAGE-4 "UI requirements come last but are never locked: they can be written at any stage and refined later"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  priority 3
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract "well defined ui requirements can be restrictive and often change": writing UI early never moves a feature past development
  contract built by construction: a feature's stage is only its written `stage` line, and nothing computes it from content, so UI written early moves nothing (kit#388)

behaviour BEH-STAGE-5 "The agent turns a note that describes a complex feature into a feature at the problem stage"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  in FEAT-NOTES
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  priority 3
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract the note's words become the problem statement's draft, and the note archives itself once folded (BEH-NOTE-11)
  contract the agent decides a note is a feature; he can move it back to a note by denying it
  contract built by the agent: his 2026-10-19 19:33Z note became FEAT-BELL and FEAT-COMMENTS, each written at the problem stage with its children inferred
  contract the agent's own process, so no test can name it; BEH-STAGE-10's test holds the other end, that a feature leaves problem once anything in it is built

behaviour BEH-STAGE-6 "Overlap between features is the agent's concern, not his"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  priority 4
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract the agent finds shared upstream dependencies between features and keeps them DRY during development; the board never asks him to
  contract built by construction: no page in Kit asks him about overlap, and a feature's card shows only its own behaviours; where two features share one, the behaviour carries both `in` lines (BEH-STAGE-5 and FEAT-NOTES)

# Was "only a feature with a stage line is on the board", my inference. His answer
# on it (kit-ui.notes.md 2026-10-20 07:13Z) replaced it with a column.
behaviour BEH-STAGE-7 "A feature with no stage line sits in an Unstaged column, so it can be found and staged"
  in FEAT-STAGES
  source inferred kit.notes.md#2026-10-19-0823
  source defined kit-ui.notes.md#2026-10-20-0713
  priority 2
  actor engineer
  when opens page:KitStages
  then sees region:KitStagesBoard
  contract "I think we need some unstated column rather than leaving it off the board so that they can be found and staged"
  contract my assumption: Unstaged is the first column, before problem, since staging a feature moves it rightwards out of it
